invariant: INV-16
file: sha512_hw.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh sha2-equiv
reason: sha512_hw.c's first round constant is one more than FIPS 180-4
  §4.2.3's, so every SHA-384 and SHA-512 digest a session computes on the
  instructions is wrong, and it agrees with no peer and with none of this
  tree's own portable digests. CBMC cannot read an intrinsic, so no proof
  covers this file, and bin/sha2_equiv_test is what holds it to sha512.c.
  The file has a body on arm64 alone, so the catch is the script, which
  builds the binary for arm64 and runs it under qemu-aarch64, whose max
  model has the instructions on every host. The lane skips without
  docker, and this then reports unguarded rather than caught.

